ROLE: systems_reviewer  VOTE: yellow
EXISTING_IMPLEMENTATIONS: [
  {system: "SGLang", url: "https://docs.sglang.ai/references/production_metrics.html", overlap: "Prometheus metrics and request tracing for serving latency/cache/queue/request spans; no online doomed-agent trajectory predictor or lead-time baseline test."},
  {system: "Langfuse", url: "https://github.com/langfuse/langfuse", overlap: "Open-source LLM application tracing, monitoring, evaluation, and debugging for agent actions; overlaps instrumentation/artifact layer, not the claimed causal early-warning mechanism."},
  {system: "AgentOps", url: "https://github.com/AgentOps-AI/agentops", overlap: "Open-source agent observability with step-by-step execution graphs, exceptions, session replay, and analytics; no evidence of matched-flag-rate early failure prediction beating confidence/difficulty."},
  {system: "LMCache", url: "https://github.com/LMCache/LMCache", overlap: "KV-cache reuse layer for vLLM instances; serving/cache mechanism only, no agent trajectory failure monitor."},
  {system: "FlashInfer", url: "https://github.com/flashinfer-ai/flashinfer", overlap: "GPU inference kernels for attention/GEMM/MoE/sampling; no overlap beyond LLM serving substrate."}
]
CONTRIBUTION_TYPE: mechanism
SCALE_REALISM: Does not yet hold at realistic workload. Evidence is L0 synthetic CPU-only simulation over 96 cells / 400 trajectories per row, not real tau-bench/AppWorld/SWE-agent traces. The strong claim fails its own baseline gate: monitor loses/ties agent self-confidence by AUC delta -0.006, 95% CI [-0.011,-0.001], and early coverage is 42.4% below the pre-registered >0.5 bar. Realistic scale gaps: real tool-error semantics, real loop detection, real information-gain extraction, actual termination timing, and real LLM confidence calibration.
RATIONALE: Prompt version v001. I found shipping OSS observability systems that already collect many required signals: SGLang exposes Prometheus metrics and OpenTelemetry request tracing; Langfuse tracks LLM calls, retrieval, embeddings, and agent actions; AgentOps provides agent execution graphs/session replay/exception handling. These make the proposed artifact partly an integration over existing telemetry, but I did not find an OSS system that already implements the exact online causal doomed-trajectory monitor with measured lead time and matched-flag-rate comparisons against self-confidence and difficulty. The surviving evidence supports only a weak measurement insight: progression observables beat generic difficulty by AUC +0.095, 95% CI [+0.087,+0.103], but the claim as written required beating both baselines and does not. Reproducibility is acceptable for L0 because pre-registration and CSV artifacts are cited, but systems contribution remains unproven until L1 real traces.
```
